WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.490
Atoms contain protons and neutrons in the nucleus, with electrons arranged in shells around it.

2
00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:10.985
Ionization means an electron is completely removed.

3
00:00:10.985 --> 00:00:18.475
Excitation means an electron moves to a higher energy level but stays in the atom.

4
00:00:18.475 --> 00:00:24.966
Inner-shell vacancies are especially important because they can lead to characteristic x-ray production.
